# laptop — Linux environment build checklist

## Base setup

- Kubuntu, workspace setup
- Brave browser
- Protonmail + ProtonPass

## Terminal stack

```sh
# zsh + oh-my-zsh + nerd font + powerlevel10k
sudo apt install zsh
sh -c "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ohmyzsh/ohmyzsh/master/tools/install.sh)"

# Core CLI tools
sudo apt install git gh cheat ripgrep htop eza glow jq ncdu asciinema \
  rsync fd-find tree watch bat
```

## Record and replay terminal sessions

```sh
asciinema rec session.cast
asciinema play session.cast
```

## Handy invocations

```sh
fdfind pattern                          # fd is 'fdfind' on Ubuntu/Kubuntu
batcat file.md                          # bat is 'batcat' on Ubuntu/Kubuntu
column -s, -t < file.csv                # pretty-print a CSV
eza --long --tree --git --icons --level=3
glow README.md                          # markdown reader
rg "search term" ~/notes                # ripgrep across docs
```

## Aliases (add to ~/.zshrc)

```sh
alias e='eza -l'
alias more='less -X'
# after editing:
source ~/.zshrc
```

## Homelab note: Tumbleweed desktop equivalents

```sh
# Same stack on the OpenSUSE Tumbleweed box uses zypper,
# and fd/bat keep their real names:
sudo zypper install git gh ripgrep htop eza glow jq ncdu asciinema fd bat tree
```

| Tool | Purpose                    |
| ---- | -------------------------- |
| glow | markdown reader            |
| eza  | modern ls                  |
| rg   | ripgrep — search in files  |
| fd   | friendlier find            |
| bat  | cat with syntax highlight  |
| ncdu | disk usage explorer        |
